WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:127826

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.036
Thanks for making it all the way
to the end of this course.

2
00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:06.039
Generative
AI is a really powerful technology.

3
00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:09.275
It's a fundamentally non-deterministic
programing paradigm.

4
00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:13.013
All of the amazing applications
you see, whether it's retrieval

5
00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:16.549
augmented generation,
or chatbots or agents

6
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.453
to bring them to production,
you'll need to make sure that they run

7
00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.155
with the level of reliability

8
00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:25.158
that we've come to expect
from deterministic software.

9
00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:28.028
Guardrails are an important tool
to do this,

10
00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:31.998
and can help you make sure that you deal
with both the average case,

11
00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:36.403
as well as the worst case
behavior of very complex genAI workflows.

12
00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.874
Validation is important
in making sure that any genAI application

13
00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.108
you build works

14
00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:46.012
as expected, and avoids the failure cases
you explored in this course,

15
00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:50.283
as well as many, many more failure cases
that you'll run into in the wild.

16
00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:51.885
You've learned the general process

17
00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.888
of building guardrails,
which is identifying problems,

18
00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:58.491
building validators to detect
when those problems occur,

19
00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:01.928
and then taking corrective actions
to mitigate those problems.

20
00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.999
Always using these guardrails around
your LLM call

21
00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:09.903
will help you make sure that your
AI is reliable and safe.

22
00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:14.274
So please take the time to explore
the validators that are available

23
00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:18.378
on the guardrails hub, and even consider
building your own guardrails

24
00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:22.315
and sharing them with the community
through our open-source projects.

25
00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.684
I can't wait to see
what you're going to build.

